  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In April 2025 testimony, James Danly said data centers, AI, and reindustrialization have brought load onto the system at an unprecedented rate that shows no signs of slowing. He described sufficient generation as critical to meet rising demand, including AI, and cited an estimate that the United States was about 18 months ahead of China in AI language-model development. Danly also said the imperative to win the AI race is clear. He identified permitting of natural gas pipelines as a major regulatory obstacle to using natural gas to address short- and intermediate-term resource adequacy.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s3",
    "s2",
    "s4"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
     "text": "In April 2025 testimony, James Danly said data centers, AI, and reindustrialization have brought load onto the system at an unprecedented rate that shows no signs of slowing.",
